-- ============================================================================
-- crude EXPERT DEEP SEED: Crude Assay & Blending, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE LEAST-COST RECIPE, and linear programming for the
-- Commercial & Trading module. An LP is an objective, rows and bounds; its optimum
-- sits on a vertex; optimal, infeasible and unbounded are all answers; a limit
-- on a ratio is a linear row; volume, mass and index are declared bases; a
-- binding specification is met exactly and the rest give quality away; the
-- shadow price of a specification is the money one unit of relief saves, per
-- unit of the property, at the margin; the marginal barrel is not the average
-- barrel.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A row's dual is not a price. optimiseBlend
-- scales it by the row's own weights and the index slope into dollars per
-- ppm, per psi, per octane number, and keeps rowPrice beside it.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A tank typed as 0 is empty, a blank maximum
-- is unlimited, and a blank cost is refused; each changes the recipe.
--
-- HELD, taught as a limit and never graded: the kernel's absolute tolerances
-- (L4). Every figure is invented and illustrative. The capstone grades six
-- four-decimal engine figures at a tolerance of 5e-5.
-- ============================================================================

values ('crude', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-linear-programme-is","title":"What a Linear Programme Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-recipe-is-a-continuous-decision","l02-an-objective-rows-and-bounds","l03-the-optimum-sits-on-a-vertex","l04-optimal-infeasible-and-unbounded","l05-two-phases"]},{"key":"m02-blending-rules-as-rows","title":"Blending Rules as Rows","lesson_keys":["l01-a-ratio-limit-becomes-a-row","l02-volume-mass-and-index","l03-the-rvp-index","l04-viscosity-on-mass-in-the-diesel-pool"]},{"key":"m03-binding-and-giveaway","title":"Binding and Giveaway","lesson_keys":["l01-the-apapa-recipe","l02-binding-specifications","l03-giveaway-is-quality-handed-over","l04-pricing-the-giveaway"]},{"key":"m04-shadow-prices","title":"Shadow Prices","lesson_keys":["l01-the-dual-of-a-row","l02-relief-per-unit-of-the-property","l03-the-index-slope","l04-the-marginal-barrel","l05-checking-a-price-by-re-solving"]},{"key":"m05-infeasible-refused-and-skipped","title":"Infeasible, Refused and Skipped","lesson_keys":["l01-infeasible-is-an-answer","l02-a-typed-zero-is-none","l03-a-blank-cost-is-refused","l04-a-specification-not-applied","l05-bounds-that-cross"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-apapa-pool-end-to-end","l02-what-is-held-and-what-the-oracles-check","l03-where-this-course-hands-over"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
